[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-7a3723d7-29ab-420f-875f-d751f6f72b41\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Track</p><strong>Wed 15 Apr 2026 14:45 - 15:00 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/icse-2026/icse-2026-venue-europa-ii\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Europa II</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track#program\" class=\"navigate\">AI for Software Engineering 6</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/miryungkim\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Miryung Kim</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"7a3723d7-29ab-420f-875f-d751f6f72b41\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>What to Retrieve for Effective Retrieval-Augmented Code Generation? An Empirical Study and Beyond</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><span class=\"pull-right\"><span title=\"Virtual Attendance\" class=\"output-badge\"><img alt=\"Virtual Attendance\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getImageFile/5a83481a-76b0-4d52-a281-ed633e8995d2/small?1776349051000\" class=\"outputimage\"/></span></span><p>Repository-level code generation remains challenging due to complex code dependencies and the limitations of large language models (LLMs) in processing long contexts. While retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) frameworks are widely adopted, the effectiveness of different retrieved information sources\u2014contextual code, APIs, and similar snippets\u2014has not been rigorously analyzed. Through an empirical study on two benchmarks, we demonstrate that in-context code and potential API information significantly enhance LLM performance, whereas retrieved similar code often introduces noise, degrading results by up to 15%. Based on the preliminary results, we propose AllianceCoder, a novel context-integrated method that employs chain-of-thought prompting to decompose user queries into implementation steps and retrieves APIs via semantic description matching. Through extensive experiments on CoderEval and RepoExec, AllianceCoder achieves state-of-the-art performance, improving Pass@1 by 10\u201320% over existing approaches.</p>\n<p></p><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/wenchaogu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Wenchao Gu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Technical University of Munich</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/juntaochen\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Juntao Chen<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Sun Yat-Sen University</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2026/yanlinwang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\